KG42.register("nodes-2ab8c55ccacf769e104196d9",{"id":"COMP-93c52ad833d04287","code":"SET036","label":"Vehicle electricity-trade payments, rewards, transfers, case-specific spread revenue and disconnection penalties","definition":"The amount rules are pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^J b_{ij}^n and Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^I (s_{ji}^n)^2/(4l_1)+r_j^{min}, respectively. After the transaction, the charging PHEV transfers energy coins to the discharging PHEV wallet according to the smart-meter record. The example calls the difference between payment and reward the auctioneer's revenue; a PHEV that suddenly disconnects in a reserved transaction must additionally bear a disconnection penalty.","layer":"L8","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"settlement.payment","concept_ids":["settlement.payment"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: buyer payment, seller reward, auctioneer differential revenue, and disconnection penalty","Amount operation: calculate payment and reward separately according to buyer bids and seller bids","Transfer operation: complete wallet payment after the transaction based on meter records","Liability rule: sudden disconnection of a scheduled transaction triggers a penalty obligation","Outputs: payment amount, reward amount, transfer, differential revenue, and penalty liability"]},"exclusions":["The local auctioneer provides the payment and reward functions","l_1>0; r_j^{min} is the seller's minimum participation reward","The payment medium is energy coins, and the recipient is the seller's wallet address","The differential revenue statement comes from an example with 35 buyers and 45 sellers; no aggregate total relationship is inferred from averages","The penalty applies to sudden disconnection of reserved vehicles within a specified scheduling period; the amount rule is not given","The formula for allocating total payment across individual seller wallets is not given"],"members":[{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Demand submissions, including requested electricity quantity and expected serving time, are sent to the LAG's transaction server. Scope: Charging-PHEV electricity requests submitted to the nearest LAG serving the localized market. Discharging PHEVs return responses about their determined selling electricity to the controller. Scope: Discharging-PHEV supply responses in the localized selling-and-buying procedure. In this example, the difference between charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards constitutes the auctioneer's benefit. Scope: Reported LAG1 parking-lot example with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging PHEVs. The auctioneer terminates the procedure and prepares to restart Algorithm 1. Scope: Participant-change handling in Algorithm 1 for the current localized P2P electricity auction. Condition: The participating PHEVs of the current localized P2P electricity trading change. The auctioneers may restart Algorithm 1 and reinitialize parameters on demand. Scope: Real-time control of localized P2P electricity trading. Condition: An unexpected event, such as abrupt disconnection of scheduled PHEVs, activates a trigger. The proposed auction is weakly budget balanced: the auctioneer does not suffer a loss while conducting it. Scope: Financial outcome for the auctioneer conducting the proposed iterative double auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Charging-PHEV electricity requests submitted to the nearest LAG serving the localized market. | Discharging-PHEV supply responses in the localized selling-and-buying procedure. | Financial outcome for the auctioneer conducting the proposed iterative double auction. | Participant-change handling in Algorithm 1 for the current localized P2P electricity auction. | Real-time control of localized P2P electricity trading. | Reported LAG1 parking-lot example with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging PHEVs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e040","v141-b-g01-e042","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24"]},"constraint_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"fc38db1516ea035caf0c82a406e6aac3e536d24b1897190d5ea29804aebe2968","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004","node_id":"settlement.payment","function":"settlement.payment","unit_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"The local auctioneer provides the charging-PHEV payment function and the discharging-PHEV reward function. Scope: Charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards in localized P2P electricity trading served by an LAG. Electricity trading precedes the charging PHEV's payment for that transaction. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment for a localized electricity transaction with a discharging PHEV. Charging PHEVs pay discharging PHEVs according to smart-meter records. Scope: Payments from charging PHEVs to discharging PHEVs for localized electricity transactions. A charging PHEV pays by transferring energy coins from its wallet to the discharging PHEV's wallet address. Scope: The payment medium and transfer method for charging-PHEV energy transactions. For charging PHEV CV_i, payment equals the sum of its buying bid prices b_{ij}^n over discharging PHEVs j. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. For discharging PHEV DV_j, the reward equals the sum of (s_{ji}^n)^2/(4l_1) over charging PHEVs i, plus a minimum reward for participation in local electricity trading. Scope: Discharging-PHEV reward schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. The abruptly disconnected PHEV is held accountable and must pay a disconnection penalty. Scope: Scheduled localized P2P electricity trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. Condition: A scheduled PHEV abruptly disconnects from its scheduled trade.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Charging-PHEV payment for a localized electricity transaction with a discharging PHEV. | Charging-PHEV payment schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. | Charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards in localized P2P electricity trading served by an LAG. | Discharging-PHEV reward schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. | Payments from charging PHEVs to discharging PHEVs for localized electricity transactions. | Scheduled localized P2P electricity trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. | The payment medium and transfer method for charging-PHEV energy transactions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e044","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g03-E09"]},"constraint_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"36f1186f681ed40f70e7ede295237785bc4e47825b209ef2b367e8491b17eef9","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010","node_id":"settlement.payment","function":"settlement.payment","unit_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["44-blockchain_phev_trading"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":"3161","section":"B. Numerical Results","anchor_text":"pp y g parking lots (see Fig. 4). We formulate electricity consumption tra behavior of PHEV as recor","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Therefore, we set the battery capacity of the PHEVs to 24 KWh. The minimum and maximum of electricity demand for charging PHEVs are [5, 10] KWh and [12, 18] KWh, respectively. The maximum of electricity supply for discharging PHEVs is [10, 20] KWh. The cost factors of cost function, i.e., l_1 and l_2 in (2), are set to 0.01 and 0.015, respectively. The average charging efficiency η is 0.8 and the average electricity transmission efficiency ρ is 0.9. The minimum reward for a discharging PHEV r_j^{min} randomly ranges from 1 to 2 dollars. The convergence threshold ε is 0.001. We take a parking lot with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging in LAG1 as an example.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"Therefore, we set the battery capacity of the PHEVs to 24 KWh. The minimum and maximum of electricity demand for charging PHEVs are [5, 10] KWh and [12, 18] KWh, respectively. The maximum of electricity supply for discharging PHEVs is [10, 20] KWh. The cost factors of cost function, i.e., l_1 and l_2 in (2), are set to 0.01 and 0.015, respectively. The average charging efficiency η is 0.8 and the average electricity transmission efficiency ρ is 0.9. The minimum reward for a discharging PHEV r_j^{min} randomly ranges from 1 to 2 dollars. The convergence threshold ε is 0.001. We take a parking lot with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging in LAG1 as an example."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":"3162","section":"B. Numerical Results","anchor_text":"g charged electricity from all the discharging PHEV converges er- when the number of iterations is 2","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 7(b)","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 7(b) shows the convergence evolution of average payment for 35 charging PHEVs and average reward of 45 discharging PHEVs. The average payment of charging PHEVs for discharging PHEVs finally converges to 2.50 dollars. And the average reward of discharging PHEVs converges to 2.04 dollars after a few iterations. The difference between payment of charging PHEVs and reward of discharging PHEVs is the benefit of the auctioneer.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"Fig. 7(b) shows the convergence evolution of average payment for 35 charging PHEVs and average reward of 45 discharging PHEVs. The average payment of charging PHEVs for discharging PHEVs finally converges to 2.50 dollars. And the average reward of discharging PHEVs converges to 2.04 dollars after a few iterations. The difference between payment of charging PHEVs and reward of discharging PHEVs is the benefit of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"A. Entities in the Double Auction Mechanism (11 1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CVi for b","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CV_i for buying energy in LAGn is B_i^n ≜ {b_{ij}^n | j ∈ Z}. All bid prices of charging PHEVs in LAGn are denoted as B^n ≜ {B_i^n | i ∈ C}. CV_i needs to solve the following optimal electricity buying problem (EB, buyer) to determine its optimal bid price: EB: max_{B_i^n} [ U_i(C_i^n) − pay_i(B_i^n) ] (8) where pay_i(B_i^n) is the payment function of CV_i given by the auctioneer.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CV_i for buying energy in LAGn is B_i^n ≜ {b_{ij}^n | j ∈ Z}. All bid prices of charging PHEVs in LAGn are denoted as B^n ≜ {B_i^n | i ∈ C}. CV_i needs to solve the following optimal electricity buying problem (EB, buyer) to determine its optimal bid price: EB: max_{B_i^n} [ U_i(C_i^n) − pay_i(B_i^n) ] (8) where pay_i(B_i^n) is the payment function of CV_i given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"j DVj solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price ","equation_id":"(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"2) Discharging PHEVs: The bid price vector of DV_j for selling electricity in LAGn is denoted as S_j^n ≜ {s_{ji}^n | i ∈ C}. The bid price matrix of selling electricity is S^n ≜ {S_j^n | j ∈ Z}. DV_j solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price as follows: ES: max_{S_j^n} [ Rew_j(S_j^n) − L_j(D_j^n) ] (9) where Rew_j(S_j^n) is a reward function of DV_j given by the auctioneer.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"2) Discharging PHEVs: The bid price vector of DV_j for selling electricity in LAGn is denoted as S_j^n ≜ {s_{ji}^n | i ∈ C}. The bid price matrix of selling electricity is S^n ≜ {S_j^n | j ∈ Z}. DV_j solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price as follows: ES: max_{S_j^n} [ Rew_j(S_j^n) − L_j(D_j^n) ] (9) where Rew_j(S_j^n) is a reward function of DV_j given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p10-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"KANG et al.: ENABLING LOCALIZED PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY TRADING AMONG exploited to design a localiz","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"In this model, an iterative double auction mechanism for charging and discharging PHEVs is presented to maximize social welfare. The LAGs work as auctioneers to carry out the double auction among PHEVs according to their bid prices, which does not require private information about PHEVs.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"In this model, an iterative double auction mechanism for charging and discharging PHEVs is presented to maximize social welfare. The LAGs work as auctioneers to carry out the double auction among PHEVs according to their bid prices, which does not require private information about PHEVs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e044","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"pected serving time to the transaction server of an LAG. The alm transaction server works as a contr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"4) Paying and Earning Energy Coins: After electricity trading, a charging PHEV pays for the energy transaction through a wallet address of a discharging PHEV, as shown in Fig. 2. The charging PHEV transfers energy coins from its wallet to the given wallet address.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"4) Paying and Earning Energy Coins: After electricity trading, a charging PHEV pays for the energy transaction through a wallet address of a discharging PHEV, as shown in Fig. 2. The charging PHEV transfers energy coins from its wallet to the given wallet address."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"n- electricity trading at hotspots: charging PHEVs, discharging ng PHEVs, and idle PHEVs. Each PHEV ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The charging PHEVs pay to the discharging PHEVs according to the records in the smart meters.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"The charging PHEVs pay to the discharging PHEVs according to the records in the smart meters."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"J r) payi(Bni ) = bnij, (15) j 9) I (snji)2 Rewj(Snj ) = + rminj . (16) 4l1 i he For stimulation, rm","equation_id":"(15),(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"B. Pricing Rules The payment function of CV_i and the reward function of DV_j are, respectively, expressed as pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^{J}b_{ij}^n, (15) Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^{I}\\frac{(s_{ji}^n)^2}{4l_1}+r_j^{\\min}. (16) For stimulation, r_j^{\\min} is a minimum reward for a discharging PHEV owing to the participation in local electricity trading.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"B. Pricing Rules The payment function of CV_i and the reward function of DV_j are, respectively, expressed as pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^{J}b_{ij}^n, (15) Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^{I}\\frac{(s_{ji}^n)^2}{4l_1}+r_j^{\\min}. (16) For stimulation, r_j^{\\min} is a minimum reward for a discharging PHEV owing to the participation in local electricity trading."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":"3160","section":"C. Algorithm Implementation","anchor_text":") multiple iterations. Here, ε determines the execution time of Algorithm 1 and accuracy of ﬁnal res","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"In addition, auctioneers monitor localized P2P electricity trading in real time. When some unexpected events happen, e.g., abrupt disconnection of scheduled PHEVs, a trigger will be activated. Then the auctioneers may restart Algorithm 1 and reinitialize parameters on demand. A new electricity trading procedure is executed in time. Besides, similar to that in [6], we consider that few PHEVs suddenly leave from scheduled trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. The abruptly disconnected PHEVs will be held accountable and will be made pay for a penalty of disconnection. This algorithm is performed with acceptable overheads in practice with low frequency of restart.","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"In addition, auctioneers monitor localized P2P electricity trading in real time. When some unexpected events happen, e.g., abrupt disconnection of scheduled PHEVs, a trigger will be activated. Then the auctioneers may restart Algorithm 1 and reinitialize parameters on demand. A new electricity trading procedure is executed in time. Besides, similar to that in [6], we consider that few PHEVs suddenly leave from scheduled trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. The abruptly disconnected PHEVs will be held accountable and will be made pay for a penalty of disconnection. This algorithm is performed with acceptable overheads in practice with low frequency of restart."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["payment_reward_transfer_and_penalty"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L8-9cfa7b26e6","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L8","ontological_kind":"payment_reward_transfer_and_penalty"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","paper_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"settlement.payment","source_occurrences":[{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Demand submissions, including requested electricity quantity and expected serving time, are sent to the LAG's transaction server. Scope: Charging-PHEV electricity requests submitted to the nearest LAG serving the localized market. Discharging PHEVs return responses about their determined selling electricity to the controller. Scope: Discharging-PHEV supply responses in the localized selling-and-buying procedure. In this example, the difference between charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards constitutes the auctioneer's benefit. Scope: Reported LAG1 parking-lot example with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging PHEVs. The auctioneer terminates the procedure and prepares to restart Algorithm 1. Scope: Participant-change handling in Algorithm 1 for the current localized P2P electricity auction. Condition: The participating PHEVs of the current localized P2P electricity trading change. The auctioneers may restart Algorithm 1 and reinitialize parameters on demand. Scope: Real-time control of localized P2P electricity trading. Condition: An unexpected event, such as abrupt disconnection of scheduled PHEVs, activates a trigger. The proposed auction is weakly budget balanced: the auctioneer does not suffer a loss while conducting it. Scope: Financial outcome for the auctioneer conducting the proposed iterative double auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Charging-PHEV electricity requests submitted to the nearest LAG serving the localized market. | Discharging-PHEV supply responses in the localized selling-and-buying procedure. | Financial outcome for the auctioneer conducting the proposed iterative double auction. | Participant-change handling in Algorithm 1 for the current localized P2P electricity auction. | Real-time control of localized P2P electricity trading. | Reported LAG1 parking-lot example with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging PHEVs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e040","v141-b-g01-e042","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24"]},"constraint_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"fc38db1516ea035caf0c82a406e6aac3e536d24b1897190d5ea29804aebe2968"},{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"The local auctioneer provides the charging-PHEV payment function and the discharging-PHEV reward function. Scope: Charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards in localized P2P electricity trading served by an LAG. Electricity trading precedes the charging PHEV's payment for that transaction. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment for a localized electricity transaction with a discharging PHEV. Charging PHEVs pay discharging PHEVs according to smart-meter records. Scope: Payments from charging PHEVs to discharging PHEVs for localized electricity transactions. A charging PHEV pays by transferring energy coins from its wallet to the discharging PHEV's wallet address. Scope: The payment medium and transfer method for charging-PHEV energy transactions. For charging PHEV CV_i, payment equals the sum of its buying bid prices b_{ij}^n over discharging PHEVs j. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. For discharging PHEV DV_j, the reward equals the sum of (s_{ji}^n)^2/(4l_1) over charging PHEVs i, plus a minimum reward for participation in local electricity trading. Scope: Discharging-PHEV reward schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. The abruptly disconnected PHEV is held accountable and must pay a disconnection penalty. Scope: Scheduled localized P2P electricity trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. Condition: A scheduled PHEV abruptly disconnects from its scheduled trade.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Charging-PHEV payment for a localized electricity transaction with a discharging PHEV. | Charging-PHEV payment schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. | Charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards in localized P2P electricity trading served by an LAG. | Discharging-PHEV reward schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules. | Payments from charging PHEVs to discharging PHEVs for localized electricity transactions. | Scheduled localized P2P electricity trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. | The payment medium and transfer method for charging-PHEV energy transactions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e044","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g03-E09"]},"constraint_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"36f1186f681ed40f70e7ede295237785bc4e47825b209ef2b367e8491b17eef9"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"In this example, the difference between charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards constitutes the auctioneer's benefit. Scope: Reported LAG1 parking-lot example with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging PHEVs.","expression":"\\mathrm{Benefit}_{\\mathrm{auctioneer}} = \\mathrm{Payment}_{\\mathrm{charging\\ PHEVs}} - \\mathrm{Reward}_{\\mathrm{discharging\\ PHEVs}}","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":"3161","section":"B. Numerical Results","anchor_text":"pp y g parking lots (see Fig. 4). We formulate electricity consumption tra behavior of PHEV as recor","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Therefore, we set the battery capacity of the PHEVs to 24 KWh. The minimum and maximum of electricity demand for charging PHEVs are [5, 10] KWh and [12, 18] KWh, respectively. The maximum of electricity supply for discharging PHEVs is [10, 20] KWh. The cost factors of cost function, i.e., l_1 and l_2 in (2), are set to 0.01 and 0.015, respectively. The average charging efficiency η is 0.8 and the average electricity transmission efficiency ρ is 0.9. The minimum reward for a discharging PHEV r_j^{min} randomly ranges from 1 to 2 dollars. The convergence threshold ε is 0.001. We take a parking lot with 35 charging PHEVs and 45 discharging in LAG1 as an example."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":"3162","section":"B. Numerical Results","anchor_text":"g charged electricity from all the discharging PHEV converges er- when the number of iterations is 2","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 7(b)","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 7(b) shows the convergence evolution of average payment for 35 charging PHEVs and average reward of 45 discharging PHEVs. The average payment of charging PHEVs for discharging PHEVs finally converges to 2.50 dollars. And the average reward of discharging PHEVs converges to 2.04 dollars after a few iterations. The difference between payment of charging PHEVs and reward of discharging PHEVs is the benefit of the auctioneer."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local auctioneer provides the charging-PHEV payment function and the discharging-PHEV reward function. Scope: Charging-PHEV payments and discharging-PHEV rewards in localized P2P electricity trading served by an LAG.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g03-E09"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"A. Entities in the Double Auction Mechanism (11 1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CVi for b","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CV_i for buying energy in LAGn is B_i^n ≜ {b_{ij}^n | j ∈ Z}. All bid prices of charging PHEVs in LAGn are denoted as B^n ≜ {B_i^n | i ∈ C}. CV_i needs to solve the following optimal electricity buying problem (EB, buyer) to determine its optimal bid price: EB: max_{B_i^n} [ U_i(C_i^n) − pay_i(B_i^n) ] (8) where pay_i(B_i^n) is the payment function of CV_i given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"j DVj solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price ","equation_id":"(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"2) Discharging PHEVs: The bid price vector of DV_j for selling electricity in LAGn is denoted as S_j^n ≜ {s_{ji}^n | i ∈ C}. The bid price matrix of selling electricity is S^n ≜ {S_j^n | j ∈ Z}. DV_j solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price as follows: ES: max_{S_j^n} [ Rew_j(S_j^n) − L_j(D_j^n) ] (9) where Rew_j(S_j^n) is a reward function of DV_j given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p10-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"KANG et al.: ENABLING LOCALIZED PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY TRADING AMONG exploited to design a localiz","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"In this model, an iterative double auction mechanism for charging and discharging PHEVs is presented to maximize social welfare. The LAGs work as auctioneers to carry out the double auction among PHEVs according to their bid prices, which does not require private information about PHEVs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Electricity trading precedes the charging PHEV's payment for that transaction. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment for a localized electricity transaction with a discharging PHEV.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e044"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e044","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"pected serving time to the transaction server of an LAG. The alm transaction server works as a contr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"4) Paying and Earning Energy Coins: After electricity trading, a charging PHEV pays for the energy transaction through a wallet address of a discharging PHEV, as shown in Fig. 2. The charging PHEV transfers energy coins from its wallet to the given wallet address."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Charging PHEVs pay discharging PHEVs according to smart-meter records. Scope: Payments from charging PHEVs to discharging PHEVs for localized electricity transactions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"n- electricity trading at hotspots: charging PHEVs, discharging ng PHEVs, and idle PHEVs. Each PHEV ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The charging PHEVs pay to the discharging PHEVs according to the records in the smart meters."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A charging PHEV pays by transferring energy coins from its wallet to the discharging PHEV's wallet address. Scope: The payment medium and transfer method for charging-PHEV energy transactions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e044"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e044","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"pected serving time to the transaction server of an LAG. The alm transaction server works as a contr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"4) Paying and Earning Energy Coins: After electricity trading, a charging PHEV pays for the energy transaction through a wallet address of a discharging PHEV, as shown in Fig. 2. The charging PHEV transfers energy coins from its wallet to the given wallet address."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For charging PHEV CV_i, payment equals the sum of its buying bid prices b_{ij}^n over discharging PHEVs j. Scope: Charging-PHEV payment schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules.","expression":"pay_i(B_i^n)=\\sum_{j=1}^{J}b_{ij}^n","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R010-X003"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E14"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"A. Entities in the Double Auction Mechanism (11 1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CVi for b","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"1) Charging PHEVs: The bid price vector of CV_i for buying energy in LAGn is B_i^n ≜ {b_{ij}^n | j ∈ Z}. All bid prices of charging PHEVs in LAGn are denoted as B^n ≜ {B_i^n | i ∈ C}. CV_i needs to solve the following optimal electricity buying problem (EB, buyer) to determine its optimal bid price: EB: max_{B_i^n} [ U_i(C_i^n) − pay_i(B_i^n) ] (8) where pay_i(B_i^n) is the payment function of CV_i given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"J r) payi(Bni ) = bnij, (15) j 9) I (snji)2 Rewj(Snj ) = + rminj . (16) 4l1 i he For stimulation, rm","equation_id":"(15),(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"B. Pricing Rules The payment function of CV_i and the reward function of DV_j are, respectively, expressed as pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^{J}b_{ij}^n, (15) Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^{I}\\frac{(s_{ji}^n)^2}{4l_1}+r_j^{\\min}. (16) For stimulation, r_j^{\\min} is a minimum reward for a discharging PHEV owing to the participation in local electricity trading."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For discharging PHEV DV_j, the reward equals the sum of (s_{ji}^n)^2/(4l_1) over charging PHEVs i, plus a minimum reward for participation in local electricity trading. Scope: Discharging-PHEV reward schedules under the local iterative double-auction pricing rules.","expression":"Rew_j(S_j^n)=\\sum_{i=1}^{I}\\frac{(s_{ji}^n)^2}{4l_1}+r_j^{\\min}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-X002","v141-c-R010-X004"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-T001","v141-c-R010-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E14"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"j DVj solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price ","equation_id":"(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"2) Discharging PHEVs: The bid price vector of DV_j for selling electricity in LAGn is denoted as S_j^n ≜ {s_{ji}^n | i ∈ C}. The bid price matrix of selling electricity is S^n ≜ {S_j^n | j ∈ Z}. DV_j solves an optimal electricity selling problem (ES, seller) to determine its optimal bid price as follows: ES: max_{S_j^n} [ Rew_j(S_j^n) − L_j(D_j^n) ] (9) where Rew_j(S_j^n) is a reward function of DV_j given by the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"3159","section":"V. ITERATIVE DOUBLE AUCTION MECHANISM","anchor_text":"J r) payi(Bni ) = bnij, (15) j 9) I (snji)2 Rewj(Snj ) = + rminj . (16) 4l1 i he For stimulation, rm","equation_id":"(15),(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"B. Pricing Rules The payment function of CV_i and the reward function of DV_j are, respectively, expressed as pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^{J}b_{ij}^n, (15) Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^{I}\\frac{(s_{ji}^n)^2}{4l_1}+r_j^{\\min}. (16) For stimulation, r_j^{\\min} is a minimum reward for a discharging PHEV owing to the participation in local electricity trading."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The abruptly disconnected PHEV is held accountable and must pay a disconnection penalty. Scope: Scheduled localized P2P electricity trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. Condition: A scheduled PHEV abruptly disconnects from its scheduled trade.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20"],"ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-2be1f33ba6-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":"3160","section":"C. Algorithm Implementation","anchor_text":") multiple iterations. Here, ε determines the execution time of Algorithm 1 and accuracy of ﬁnal res","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"In addition, auctioneers monitor localized P2P electricity trading in real time. When some unexpected events happen, e.g., abrupt disconnection of scheduled PHEVs, a trigger will be activated. Then the auctioneers may restart Algorithm 1 and reinitialize parameters on demand. A new electricity trading procedure is executed in time. Besides, similar to that in [6], we consider that few PHEVs suddenly leave from scheduled trades in parking lots during a specified scheduling time period. The abruptly disconnected PHEVs will be held accountable and will be made pay for a penalty of disconnection. This algorithm is performed with acceptable overheads in practice with low frequency of restart."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X001","symbol":"b_{ij}^n","meaning":"Buying bid price submitted to the LAG auctioneer by charging PHEV CV_i for discharging PHEV DV_j in LAG n; it is an input to the charging-PHEV payment function.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real number","unit":null,"indices":["i ∈ C","j ∈ Z","n ∈ ι"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E00"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X002","symbol":"s_{ji}^n","meaning":"Selling bid price submitted to the LAG auctioneer by discharging PHEV DV_j for charging PHEV CV_i in LAG n; it is an input to the discharging-PHEV reward function.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real number","unit":null,"indices":["j ∈ Z","i ∈ C","n ∈ ι"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E00"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X003","symbol":"pay_i(B_i^n)","meaning":"Payment amount of charging PHEV CV_i as a function of its buying-bid vector B_i^n, given by the auctioneer's payment function.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued payment amount","unit":null,"indices":["i ∈ C","n ∈ ι"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X003"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X004","symbol":"Rew_j(S_j^n)","meaning":"Reward amount of discharging PHEV DV_j as a function of its selling-bid vector S_j^n, given by the auctioneer's reward function.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued reward amount","unit":null,"indices":["j ∈ Z","n ∈ ι"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X004"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-T001","symbol":"l_1","meaning":"Positive cost factor of the discharging-PHEV cost function, also used in the denominator of the discharging-PHEV reward function.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"l_1 > 0"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-T002","symbol":"r_j^{\\min}","meaning":"Minimum reward for discharging PHEV DV_j owing to participation in local electricity trading.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"dollars (numerical study)","indices":["j ∈ Z"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E23"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T002"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","stage":"L8","subtype":"payment_reward_transfer_and_penalty","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"The amount rules are pay_i(B_i^n)=∑_{j=1}^J b_{ij}^n and Rew_j(S_j^n)=∑_{i=1}^I (s_{ji}^n)^2/(4l_1)+r_j^{min}, respectively. After the transaction, the charging PHEV transfers energy coins to the discharging PHEV wallet according to the smart-meter record. The example calls the difference between payment and reward the auctioneer's revenue; a PHEV that suddenly disconnects in a reserved transaction must additionally bear a disconnection penalty.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: buyer payment, seller reward, auctioneer differential revenue, and disconnection penalty","Amount operation: calculate payment and reward separately according to buyer bids and seller bids","Transfer operation: complete wallet payment after the transaction based on meter records","Liability rule: sudden disconnection of a scheduled transaction triggers a penalty obligation","Outputs: payment amount, reward amount, transfer, differential revenue, and penalty liability"],"variation_fields":["The local auctioneer provides the payment and reward functions","l_1>0; r_j^{min} is the seller's minimum participation reward","The payment medium is energy coins, and the recipient is the seller's wallet address","The differential revenue statement comes from an example with 35 buyers and 45 sellers; no aggregate total relationship is inferred from averages","The penalty applies to sudden disconnection of reserved vehicles within a specified scheduling period; the amount rule is not given","The formula for allocating total payment across individual seller wallets is not given"],"constraint_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007"],"paper_id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"settlement.payment","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/180"});
